      "text": "Visitors enter an amusement park at the rate \\( R(t) = 4 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{4} \\right)} + 10 \\) people per hour, where t is measured in hours for \\( 0 \\le t \\le 5 \\). The park holds 70 people at time \\( t = 0 \\). During the same time, visitors leave the park at the rate \\( D(t) = t + 5 \\) people per hour. Using a calculator, find the total number of people that arrive during the time interval \\( 1 \\le t \\le 4 \\). Show the setup, and give the value correct to three decimal places.",
